---@class github.checks.UpdateRequest
---@field owner string The account owner of the repository. The name is not case sensitive.
---@field repo string The name of the repository without the `.git` extension. The name is not case sensitive.
---@field check_run_id number The unique identifier of the check run.
---@field name? string The name of the check. For example, "code-coverage".
---@field details_url? string The URL of the integrator's site that has the full details of the check.
---@field external_id? string A reference for the run on the integrator's system.
---@field started_at? string This is a timestamp in [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`.
---@field status? github.checks.UpdateRequestStatus|string The current status of the check run. Only GitHub Actions can set a status of `waiting`, `pending`, or `requested`.
---@field conclusion? github.checks.UpdateRequestConclusion|string **Required if you provide `completed_at` or a `status` of `completed`**. The final conclusion of the check. **Note:** Providing `conclusion` will automatically set the `status` parameter to `completed`. You cannot change a check run conclusion to `stale`, only GitHub can set this.
---@field completed_at? string The time the check completed. This is a timestamp in [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`.
---@field output? github.checks.UpdateRequestOutput Check runs can accept a variety of data in the `output` object, including a `title` and `summary` and can optionally provide descriptive details about the run.
---@field actions? github.checks.UpdateRequestActionsList Possible further actions the integrator can perform, which a user may trigger. Each action includes a `label`, `identifier` and `description`. A maximum of three actions are accepted. To learn more about check runs and requested actions, see "[Check runs and requested actions](https://docs.github.com/rest/guides/using-the-rest-api-to-interact-with-checks#check-runs-and-requested-actions)."

---@class github.checks.UpdateRequestActionsItem
---@field label string The text to be displayed on a button in the web UI. The maximum size is 20 characters.
---@field description string A short explanation of what this action would do. The maximum size is 40 characters.
---@field identifier string A reference for the action on the integrator's system. The maximum size is 20 characters.

---Possible further actions the integrator can perform, which a user may trigger. Each action includes a `label`, `identifier` and `description`. A maximum of three actions are accepted. To learn more about check runs and requested actions, see "[Check runs and requested actions](https://docs.github.com/rest/guides/using-the-rest-api-to-interact-with-checks#check-runs-and-requested-actions)."
---@alias github.checks.UpdateRequestActionsList github.checks.UpdateRequestActionsItem[]

---**Required if you provide `completed_at` or a `status` of `completed`**. The final conclusion of the check.
